WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.369
[music playing]

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.809
- It's snowing out, a little
snowing, white Christmas.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:20.353
- I know it's going
to happen any day now.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.590
- So the plan that they came
up with was rather ingenious.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.259
They decided to take
Paul Castellano out

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.162
by luring him to one of
his favorite restaurants

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:32.165
with captains that he
absolutely trusted.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.434
Their scheme was
all the shooters--

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.336
and they had many of
them because they wanted

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.271
to be able to pull this
off-- were going to be

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.607
in trench coats, Russian hats.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:44.144
You see that a lot in New
York and it's just so nothing,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.246
no one's really going to
pay attention to anything.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.181
If anything, they'll
focus on, well

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.283
it was a guy with a trench
coat and a Russian hat,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.851
I can't tell you
anything else about him.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.687
One of the busiest sections
of midtown Manhattan,

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:59.125
4 o'clock in the afternoon,
around the holidays.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.994
- So John Gotti who
was in the car up

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.229
the corner with Sammy the Bull.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.832
He hated Paul so much
that he wanted to see

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.100
him laying in the street.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.874
- I happened to be
with another guy.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.544
I was at dinner at his house
sitting at the kitchen table,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.646
and he had a little
television on the table.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.922
And while I was
sitting eating, we get

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.491
some 911 texts on our beepers.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.226
Back in those days
it was beepers.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:41.534
And I kept getting
them, 911, 911.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.970
And behind the 911,
I'm getting 98.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:47.307
That means come to the club
on 98 Street, the Bergin.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.878
So I know something happened.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:01:59.986
It's all over the news.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.789
It's flashed everywhere
that Paul Castellano was hit

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:05.124
in front of Sparks Steak House.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.560
- Big Paul Castellano,
reputed godfather

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.462
of the Gambino
family, was on his way

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.164
to a Manhattan steak house.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.866
As he stepped from
his black Lincoln,

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.502
three men wearing fur hats
and trench coats suddenly

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:19.272
appeared, pulled guns, pumped
six bullets into Castellano,

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:22.141
and six into his top
capo, Thomas Belotti,

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.110
and then calmly walked away.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:30.116
- I was upstairs in my room, and
all of a sudden on the news I'm

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:34.187
hearing Paul
Castellano, mob boss,

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.756
is killed outside
Sparks Steak House.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.325
And I'm thinking wow,
who could have done this?

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.765
- After the hit, Sammy Gravano
and John Gotti drove the car

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.935
down the street, and they slowed
up and looked at the bodies

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.137
and kept on going.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.373
[police chatter]

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.478
- Because he was a gangster.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:01.381
And he wanted to be there
and see it for his own eyes.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.186
And then John was the boss.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.698
- The old time mob
bosses, you see,

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.034
you know, they ruled
with an iron fist

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.569
covered with a velvet glove.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.771
Well Gotti saw no
need for the glove,

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.272
that's what it came down to.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:29.375
This was a hostile takeover
in every sense of the word.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:35.348
- After he was killed
and John became the boss,

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.318
all the heroin dealers that
were around John all got

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.485
straightened out.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:54.801
- Gotti was a boss who
reflected the times.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.737
He was always grabbing and
reaching for more and more.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:08.014
- So by the time we
reach about 1986, 1987,

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:11.618
we expand the heroin business
into the cocaine business.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.456
I have Colombian connections.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.492
So we're coming
in from Colombia,

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:24.097
there's loads coming in from
Miami, coming in from Detroit.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.906
- The allure was money,
and very easy money.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:37.510
If you've got the connections,
it's about the logistics.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.312
It was money.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.014
- So we go out to
the Hamptons, Fire

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.050
Island, party, drink, broads.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:46.986
Champagne flowing from
the morning till night.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:51.658
Listen, when you have keys to
the city like John Gotti did.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:55.862
He was arrogant, he didn't
care that he broke every rule.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.731
- You know this is supposed
to be, Cosa Nostra, our thing.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:03.002
When John Gotti took over,
it was no longer our thing,

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.139
it was my thing.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.675
- His transformation
was like a caterpillar

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.110
turning into a butterfly.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.546
All the sudden he's
wearing $3,000 ties,

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:16.983
and the cocoon opens, and
out comes the Dapper Don.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.217
- He's out and about.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.086
He's good with a quip
and a sound bite.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.888
- Why don't you just
behave yourself?

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:22.889
- I'm behaving myself.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.424
- You're not behaving yourself.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.193
- John Gotti changes the whole
dynamic of organized crime.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.196
No longer the old Sicilian
style, make money not

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.564
headlines, stay in the shadows.

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.533
The idea was what's the
point of being a gangster

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.268
if nobody knows where you are?

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.037
- Every 4th of July, he
throws a free fireworks

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:40.840
bash for the neighborhood.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.341
When police have
tried to stop it,

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.143
the crowds have
driven them back.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.980
Gotti is somewhat of
a local hero here.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:51.417
- Ironically, the neighborhood
thinks John Gotti is keeping

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.920
the drug dealers out of here.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.688
Yet John Gotti is a drug dealer.

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.791
But he's not the guy peddling
it on the street, right?

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.694
So it's the perception, he's
saving us from drug dealers.

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:02.695
No he's not.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:09.035
- Gotti was every day in
your face, look at me,

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:10.403
I'm a gangster doing this.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.506
And that drives law enforcement.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.878
[music playing]

